WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.640
Welcome to ARC, the Advising and
Registration Companion AI Powered Agent.

00:06.000 --> 00:10.515
ARC was designed to help University of
South Carolina students obtain answers to

00:10.540 --> 00:14.340
frequently asked questions about
advising and registration processes,

00:14.580 --> 00:15.900
procedures, and requirements.

00:18.358 --> 00:19.358
Let’s dive in!

00:19.598 --> 00:23.258
ARC is designed to provide
information specific to the end user.

00:23.718 --> 00:26.978
The first step is to guide the user
through selecting their program.

00:27.518 --> 00:30.498
Users can search for their major
or use the dropdown features.

00:31.018 --> 00:33.918
For those undecided, we have
an option for general guidance.

00:34.578 --> 00:38.993
Once a major is selected, the tool
confirms it is focused on the content for

00:39.018 --> 00:40.018
that major.

00:40.158 --> 00:43.153
Notice the switch major option
in the top right corner.

00:43.178 --> 00:48.473
The ability to switch majors is available
to the end user at all times to allow

00:48.498 --> 00:50.798
users to potentially
compare different majors.

00:53.354 --> 00:57.309
At this point, users can ask predefined
questions that are listed to help them

00:57.334 --> 00:59.894
get started, or they can
ask their own questions.

01:02.274 --> 01:06.029
It is important to note that data is
input and reviewed by subject matter

01:06.054 --> 01:08.534
experts from three levels
of the organization:

01:08.954 --> 01:13.549
university wide administrative content,
college specific content, and major

01:13.574 --> 01:14.574
specific content.

01:15.334 --> 01:19.869
ARC intelligently analyzes all levels
of content associated with the major and

01:19.894 --> 01:24.329
returns an answer which also includes
confidence levels, sources referenced, and

01:24.354 --> 01:25.354
important notes.

01:26.014 --> 01:30.689
All data must have an owner, appropriate
scope tags, effective terms, and Source

01:30.714 --> 01:31.714
URLs.

01:33.944 --> 01:36.144
Let’s get into a couple examples:

01:37.098 --> 01:40.413
In this example we have selected
the Bachelor of Music major and are

01:40.438 --> 01:42.758
highlighting a question about
progression requirements.

01:43.138 --> 01:46.953
ARC searched the source content and
returned a response that is found in the

01:46.978 --> 01:48.138
major level content.

01:50.416 --> 01:54.291
In our next example, the user asks about
a deadline for dropping a class without

01:54.316 --> 01:55.316
a W.

01:55.396 --> 01:59.331
ARC appropriately returned the policy
details found in the university wide

01:59.356 --> 02:00.796
administrative data level.

02:05.929 --> 02:09.444
In the final examples, the user asks
a question that highlights the safety

02:09.469 --> 02:10.909
boundaries designed in ARC.

02:11.309 --> 02:13.809
The user asks what
elective is the easiest.

02:14.429 --> 02:18.444
ARC will refuse questions unrelated to
its purpose and will return a generic

02:18.469 --> 02:20.309
response redirecting the user.

02:21.009 --> 02:24.324
If the user were to ask a question
concerning information not in the source

02:24.349 --> 02:27.904
data, ARC will not provide responses
for questions that it does not have

02:27.929 --> 02:31.544
adequate source information and points
to relevant contact information for the

02:31.569 --> 02:32.569
advising team.

02:34.820 --> 02:36.500
Thank you for learning more about ARC!
